// A header field, RFC 9110 §5:
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#section-5
//
// A name and a value as octets, and nothing else. Both header compressions produce and
// consume these, so HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 speak of a header list in one type — a package of
// its own so neither compression has to be linked to name the other's output.
